n pinned; output passes `scanner.DecodeFindings`, every path passes `checkFilePath`, and `redact.Builtin()` finds nothing in it\n- [ ] Canary test: a unique marker in every non-allowlisted field (`Raw`, `RawV2`, `Redacted`, `SecretParts`, `ExtraData`, `StructuredData`, `VerificationError`, `email`, `repository`, `repository_local_path`, `DetectorDescription`) appears nowhere in stdout, stderr or the temp dir, including after a run killed mid-stream. Committed fixtures use canary strings that are not credential-shaped\n- [ ] Each fail-closed case exits non-zero with empty stdout; recorded argv contains `--no-verification --no-update --no-ignore-tag --fail-on-scan-errors --json` and none of the forbidden flags\n- [ ] `exclude-paths` and `allow` (fingerprint, comments) work; a missing tool exits 2\n- [ ] Pipeline: `route: needs-human` files with `ard:needs-human` and no `ard:pending`, joins work, the stale closer leaves the issue alone, a secret removed from HEAD autocloses it; the pre-filing scan fails a run whose body holds a token; `ard config check` validates `route`\n- [ ] Integration (`integration` tag, `ARD_TRUFFLEHOG_BIN`): a temp repo built at run time (tokens assembled from pieces) with one key in two files, one URI with a password, one excluded path and one symlink to a planted secret outside the tree; reports exactly the expected fingerprints, no planted value in stdout or stderr, a second run is identical\n- [ ] Docker integration test (like `cve_docker_integration_test.go`) runs the image with `--network none`, a `:ro` mount and `--cap-drop ALL`, with the same assertions\n- [ ] The starter tree and `ard config check` accept the role; `ard init` proposes it with `scan` committed as 0755\n- [ ] Proposal and CLAUDE.md updated in the same PR; `#53` gets a one-line note that scanners routed to `needs-human` are excluded from the Gate 3 metric; `make lint test` passes\n\n**Design:** [docs/proposal.md: Scanners](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/main/docs